# PcManager Project Standards

## Architecture
- Follow SOLID in all layers and components.
- Keep classes focused (SRP) and depend on abstractions (DIP).
- Prefer extension over modification (OCP) through handlers/strategies.

## Development process
- Use TDD cycle: Red -> Green -> Refactor.
- Use NUnit for all tests (unit and integration).
- Do not merge features without tests for core behavior.

## Engineering principles
- Apply KISS: prefer the simplest correct implementation.
- Apply DRY: remove duplication when repetition is stable and meaningful.
- Apply YAGNI: do not implement speculative features.

## C# coding conventions
- Public classes and public methods must include XML documentation in Russian.
- Code comments should be in Russian and only where they add value.
- Follow C# naming rules from ktaranov naming convention:
  - PascalCase for namespaces, classes, methods, properties, enums.
  - camelCase for parameters and local variables.
  - Prefix interfaces with `I`.
  - Private fields can use `_camelCase`.
  - Avoid abbreviations unless common (`Id`, `Uri`, `Xml`).
  - Do not use Hungarian notation.
  - Keep enum names singular (except `[Flags]` enums).

## Security and privacy
- Never commit secrets, tokens, passwords, private keys, or PII.
- Use environment variables or secret storage for sensitive values.
- Sanitize logs: never print raw tokens or sensitive payloads.

## Documentation structure
- Keep root `README.md` as a documentation index and quick start.
- Store detailed documentation in `docs/`.

## Versions policy
- Use latest stable .NET and package versions.
- Avoid preview packages in production unless explicitly approved.

## Commit conventions
- Use Conventional Commits types only: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`.
- Commit message language: concise English.
- Follow ktaranov git comment structure:
  - Subject line first, capitalized, without trailing period, target 50 chars (max 80).
  - Empty line between subject and body.
  - Body explains what changed and why (not only how).
- Optional flags when applicable: `!!!` (breaking), `DB` (database changes), `WIP` (work in progress; never merge).
